{"ts_utc": "2026-05-12T16:11:43.551524Z", "run_id": "20260512_161114_rag_L3_B7_dd196b", "seq": 5, "event": "generation.completed", "payload": {"answer": "Road transport and infrastructure issues were discussed in Parliament, specifically regarding:\n\n* Allocation of roads to certain constituencies, with only two roads allocated to the Deputy Minister for Finance's constituency in the Eastern Region [dff4571f96a0c9d7265906fba17679b935006ecfb10abc19742dff121af4c1f3:59].\n* The District Road Improvement Programme (DRIP) and the need for more roads to be constructed [dff4571f96a0c9d7265906fba17679b935006ecfb10abc19742dff121af4c1f3:59].\n* Delays in payment or execution of road projects, with institutions working against the country's interest [c5c72f37c302ef9b1452d16465c23ef330167c1b086da25efca6cdf9bd4bd0e3:10].\n* Poor quality of roads and the need for better management of the road sector [217f0c90ad02f0f71a5a8fd57ce4d2deb97070e6c3fc77f4be86456c6f3723c2:24].\n* Inequitable distribution of national resources, with some regions receiving less funding for roads than others [217f0c90ad02f0f71a5a8fd57ce4d2deb97070e6c3fc77f4be86456c6f3723c2:24].\n* The need to ensure that every constituency gets a fair share of the national cake and has access to good roads [217f0c90ad02f0f71a5a8fd57ce4d2deb97070e6c3fc77f4be86456c6f3723c2:24].", "answer_sha256": "9268e03edd95cdacc3c72a844dda733b94a29b4b307d06f3cc13b7d4b5db3139"}, "prev_hash": "f215efeea9de232d5585c12a8c7ef025a505502ae79f8f742030c0e09edfbd0f", "event_hash": "aa30fca978806293cde445680cdebb6ef161761aff3f60a4bde8c5957601e0b1"}
